{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/master/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "pmat",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/paiml/pmat",
          "version": "3.30.0",
          "rules": []
        }
      },
      "invocations": [
        {
          "executionSuccessful": true,
          "commandLine": "git diff ba09f72af5 7218961ef9 -- . ':!evidence/pr-review'"
        }
      ],
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "PRREV-SCOPE-001",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Carried forward, updated for the new head 7218961ef9: this run reads IN FULL the 3-commit delta since ba09f72af5 (7cc5f7d4f3 setsid-wrap fix, 7218961ef9 supported.yaml re-derive, 00d9872441 evidence-only minisig commit) -- 2 files changed outside evidence/pr-review (ci/sections.yml, evidence/models/supported.yaml), 42 insertions/42 deletions. The wider PR's ~726 files not touched by this delta retain the scope limitation recorded at d57f897/ba09f72a and are NOT re-read this run; their disposition is carried forward unchanged."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": ["git", "diff", "--stat", "ba09f72af521327a5f657c06eb4368d2d720fd25", "7218961ef990d1c8d6a5af9817ea3da40f25d287", "--", ".", ":!evidence/pr-review"],
            "exit_code": 0,
            "failure_scenario": "A reader could assume this receipt re-reviewed the full PR; it reviewed the 3-commit/2-file delta plus everything the prior receipts already sampled, not the whole diff again.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "PRREV-GUARDSTEP-ISO-001",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "RESOLVED this run: 7cc5f7d4f3 wraps the 6 previously-bare guard/mutation invocations in the 'lean guards (leanchecker scoped, modules reachable) + their mutation sets' CI step under `setsid --wait`, matching every other guard step in ci/sections.yml. Independently re-ran scripts/check_guard_steps_isolated.sh against the live tree (no --self-test): PASS, every direct guard invocation in 25 workflow(s) runs under setsid --wait. Also ran the script's own --self-test (14 rows including a real mutant case -- 'ci/sections.yml with one wrapper removed is refused'): 0 failed, so the guard's positive result is not vacuous -- it demonstrably can flag exactly this class of defect and did, per the CI run context given (36496045871 on 7eb331468c), before this fix landed."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": ["bash", "scripts/check_guard_steps_isolated.sh"],
            "exit_code": 0,
            "failure_scenario": "Without the wrap, a guard invocation running outside setsid --wait can be orphaned by a killed parent process group and leave residue or a false green; the mutant row in the script's own self-test proves the check would have caught the pre-fix state.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "PRREV-MODELS-YAML-001",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "7218961ef9 re-derives evidence/models/supported.yaml after a README.md edit shifted line numbers. Diffed the full change: every hunk is a `README.md:<N>` citation-line-number update (verified by grepping the diff's added/removed lines with README.md:[0-9]+ stripped out -- zero non-line-number lines remained, i.e. no model name/family/size/cited_by_count changed). Independently re-ran `bash scripts/derive_model_manifest.sh --check`: PASS, derive_model_manifest: evidence/models/supported.yaml equals its derivation (24 models). No defect found."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": ["bash", "scripts/derive_model_manifest.sh", "--check"],
            "exit_code": 0,
            "failure_scenario": "A citation-only re-derive that actually dropped or reassigned a model's cited_by entries would be indistinguishable from a cosmetic line-shift without diffing the non-line-number content and re-running the derivation gate.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "PRREV-SIG-001",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "00d9872441 commits the CI signer's .minisig for the ba09f72af5 receipt (evidence/pr-review/4587/ba09f72af521327a5f657c06eb4368d2d720fd25/receipt.intoto.jsonl.minisig), excluded from the patch-id as instructed. Independently verified: `minisign -V -q -m <dir>/receipt.intoto.jsonl -p .github/pr-review.pub -x <dir>/receipt.intoto.jsonl.minisig` exits 0. Also ran `bash scripts/pr_review_sign_receipt.sh --self-test` (verify-only mode, does not sign this receipt): 14 passed, 0 failed, including the 'a signature that fails verification is DELETED, not left on disk' row, so the verify path is not vacuous."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": ["minisign", "-V", "-q", "-m", "evidence/pr-review/4587/ba09f72af521327a5f657c06eb4368d2d720fd25/receipt.intoto.jsonl", "-p", ".github/pr-review.pub", "-x", "evidence/pr-review/4587/ba09f72af521327a5f657c06eb4368d2d720fd25/receipt.intoto.jsonl.minisig"],
            "exit_code": 0,
            "failure_scenario": "An unverifiable or mismatched signature committed as evidence would be worse than none -- it would look like a signed receipt to a downstream reader while proving nothing; the explicit re-verify against the committed pubkey rules this out.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "PRREV-GUARD-MUTSET-001",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Carried forward, disposition unaffected by this delta: c1e4d195c5's 3 committed mutation sets (facade_compat, lean_modules_reachable, leanchecker_scoped) were already verified 100% (17/17, 18/18, 31/31) at the ba09f72a review. This delta's ci/sections.yml change only re-wraps the same 6 invocations in setsid --wait; it does not alter the mutation sets' content or counts. Not re-run this session (no change to the scripts themselves in this delta) -- re-verified only that the files are byte-unchanged since ba09f72a via git diff --stat above showing no scripts/mutate_*_guard.sh entries."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "rationale": "git diff --stat ba09f72af5..7218961ef9 lists only ci/sections.yml and evidence/models/supported.yaml; the 3 mutation-set scripts are not in the delta, so their prior 100%-kill measurement stands without re-running.",
            "failure_scenario": "If any mutation-set script had been touched by this delta, its prior measurement would need re-running; it was not touched.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "PRREV-VERSION-001",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Carried forward, unaffected: ba09f72af5's bump-version.sh facade-pin fix was verified at the ba09f72a review (10/10 self-test rows) and is not touched by this delta (bump-version.sh does not appear in git diff --stat ba09f72af5..7218961ef9)."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "rationale": "Not in the delta's changed-file list; no re-check needed.",
            "failure_scenario": "n/a -- unchanged file.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "PRREV-MUTANTS-001",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "PR1-MUTANTS HARD-STOP CARRIED FORWARD, UNCHANGED and NOT RE-MEASURED against this head, per explicit instruction: the base_sha is unchanged (ef72c05809) and this 3-commit/2-file delta (a CI wrapper fix, a citation-line re-derive, and an evidence-only .minisig commit) touches no application logic in the 3555-in-diff-mutant surface measured at d57f897/carried at ba09f72a. It is an operator-declared, non-waivable HARD-STOP: merging against a 60-mutant CI cap while the underlying diff contains 3555 in-diff mutants means the mutation gate cannot meaningfully exercise the vast majority of changed logic. This finding alone continues to force the verdict to something other than a clean approve, regardless of every other finding on this delta being resolved or clean. Per the operator ruling relayed for this review, this is NOT a fix target on this branch and the cap must not be raised; it is escalated to the operator as a HARD-STOP."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "rationale": "Carried forward from the ba09f72a receipt's own measured cargo-mutants --in-diff --list run (3555 in-diff mutants vs cap 60); not re-run this session per explicit task instruction that it is a standing BLOCK, not a re-measurement target.",
            "failure_scenario": "Merging this PR while the mutation gate's cap (60) covers under 2% of the diff's in-diff mutant surface (3555) means most changed application logic ships with zero mutation coverage in CI.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "PRREV-DUP-001",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Carried forward unchanged: the full duplication horizon sweep (siblings + merge_base_to_main) was not run this session either. duplication_coverage remains 'none' across every surface. This delta (a CI wrapper fix, a re-derived citation manifest, and a committed .minisig) presents no plausible new duplication surface, but the sweep itself was not executed."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "rationale": "No new duplication sweep was performed this run; restating the prior honest gap rather than dropping it.",
            "failure_scenario": "A near-duplicate re-implementation anywhere in the 728-file diff would go undetected without this sweep.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "nvidia-cuda-docs",
          "informationUri": "https://developer.nvidia.com/cuda-toolkit"
        }
      },
      "invocations": [
        {
          "executionSuccessful": false,
          "toolExecutionNotifications": [
            {
              "level": "error",
              "message": {
                "text": "Carried forward unchanged: mcp__nvidia-cuda-docs__search_cuda_docs not present in this session's tool set. Not re-checked this run -- the 2-file delta (ci/sections.yml, evidence/models/supported.yaml) touches no CUDA-adjacent path."
              },
              "properties": {
                "grounding": "asserted",
                "rationale": "No new path in the delta matches the S3.B trigger.",
                "exit_code": 0
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "PRREV-CUDA-001",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Carried forward unchanged: the S3.B path trigger's 2 false-positive files (cuda_simd_scores.rs.txt, fp8-interchange-v1.lean) are untouched by this delta. Disposition stands."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": ["git", "diff", "--stat", "ba09f72af521327a5f657c06eb4368d2d720fd25", "7218961ef990d1c8d6a5af9817ea3da40f25d287"],
            "exit_code": 0,
            "failure_scenario": "If the delta had touched either fixture file, the disposition would need re-checking; it does not.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "crux",
          "informationUri": "internal:crux"
        }
      },
      "invocations": [
        {
          "executionSuccessful": true
        }
      ],
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "PRREV-CRUX-001",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Carried forward unchanged: the 2-file delta (ci/sections.yml, evidence/models/supported.yaml) adds no new CLI-facing command surface, so the prior crux_coverage='none' disposition is unaffected and carried forward rather than re-swept."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "rationale": "Neither changed file is a contracts/apr-cli-commands-v1.yaml or crux-adjacent surface.",
            "failure_scenario": "If the delta had added a new CLI-facing command, the crux disposition would need re-checking; it does not.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
